course: dictionary
lesson: 3207
title: Enhancement and fancy words
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: An enhancement is an improvement that makes something better, stronger or more attractive. Software can get an enhancement that adds new features, and a photo can get image enhancement that makes it clearer. «In politics, someone caught saying something false may say they "misspoke", and a new tax can be called "revenue enhancement".» The sentence is about words that sound nicer than the thing they describe.
explain: Enhancement is a formal word. Use the clues around it to work out what it means: software, photos and performance are all things that can get better. In everyday talk you can say "improvement" instead.
explain: Be careful with a word that sounds positive. «Revenue enhancement» sounds like something good, but a new tax is usually something people do not want. The writer is showing that a pleasant word can be used to make a thing sound better than it really is. Ask yourself: who chose this word, and why?
fact: An enhancement is an improvement that makes something better, stronger or more attractive.
fact: Enhancement is the act of making something better.
fact: In everyday talk, say "improvement" instead of "enhancement".
fact: «Image enhancement» makes photos clearer, and «a software enhancement» adds new features.
fact: A fancy word can make something sound nicer than it really is, so read the whole sentence before you believe it.
exercise: The game got a big enhancement, with new levels and faster loading. What does enhancement mean here? | A slow update that makes the game worse | * An improvement that makes the game better | A new game for two players | A mistake that stops the game working
exercise: Ruby says enhancement is a big word. What everyday word could she use instead? | amusement | disappointment | * improvement | argument
exercise: «In politics, a new tax can be called "revenue enhancement".» What is the writer hinting? | * The word can make a tax sound nicer than it really is | The tax is free for everyone | The word means exactly the same as "lower tax" | Revenue is a type of fruit
test: Which sentence uses enhancement correctly? | Enhancement is the name of the dog who runs very fast. | I had an enhancement for lunch and went to bed early. | * The app got an enhancement that fixed bugs and added a dark mode. | The app got an enhancement that fixed bugs and added a dark mode.
test: Which word is the closest everyday swap for "image enhancement" in «The team used image enhancement to make the old photo clearer»? | making the photo older | making the photo smaller | making the photo quieter | * making the photo better
exam: In «A new tax can be called "revenue enhancement"», what should a careful reader do before believing the word? | Stop reading the book forever | * Think about who chose the word and whether it makes something sound nicer than it is | Believe it, because fancy words are always true | Look up the word revenue only and ignore the rest
